  <text>
      <body>
         <div type="page" n="1">
            
            <docDate when="1909-03-08">March 8, 1909. Monday</docDate>
            
            <figure>
               <graphic url="1909-03-08.jpg">
                  <desc>The original calender page for March 8, 1909</desc>
               </graphic>
               <figDesc> A huge, red question mark</figDesc>
            </figure>
            
            <p>
               <unclear>Perhaps This is the day,</unclear> <gap reason="illegible"/>
            </p>
         </div>
         
         <div type="page" n="2">
            
            <docDate when="1909-03-12">March 12, 1909. Friday</docDate>
            
            <figure>
               <graphic url="1909-03-12.jpg">
                  <desc>The original calender page for March 12, 1909</desc>
               </graphic>
               <figDesc> A hand-drawn woman wearing a dark skirt and hat, standing on two yellow snowshoes decorated with red marks.</figDesc>
            </figure>
            
            <p>
               <name>MOLLY</name> ON <objectName>SNOWSHOES</objectName> THAT <name>MR.WEIR</name> GOT. PRETTY PICTURE IS IT NOT?!
            </p>
            <p>
               Love from <name>molly</name>
            </p>
         </div>
         
         <div type="page" n="3">
            
            <docDate when="1909-03-17">March 12, 1909. Friday St.Patrick's Day</docDate>
            
            <figure>
               <graphic url="1909-03-17.jpg">
                  <desc>The original calender page for March 17, 1909</desc>
               </graphic>
               <figDesc>
                  Two snakes on the top of the paragraph, one was bent over, the other curled up. Some clover drwan in the whole page. A hand-drawn industrial building with several smokestacks producing dark smoke at bottom of the page.
               </figDesc>
            </figure>
            
            <p>
               ST.PATRICK WAS A USEFUF SAiNT <lb/>
               HE FRIDHTENED ALL THE SNAKES AWAT-<lb/>
               I WISH HE'D TRY HIS ART OF <label type="underline"><damage>S</damage>MOKE</label><lb/>
               AROUND THE HAMMERMiLL SOME DAY!<lb/>
            </p>
            <p>
               The Hammermill <unclear>really <gap reason="illegible"/> smoke!</unclear>
            </p>
         </div>
      </body>
  </text>
